Error [E0201]: ExpiringSecret loan `borrowed` cannot be moved
  --> expiring_secret_loan_rejects_move_variadic_and_drop_paths.jet:12:18
    |
 12 |         consume(^borrowed)
    |                  ^^^^^^^^
 Why: The callback receives temporary read access; moving, changing, or dropping it could let the credential escape its expiry boundary
 Fix: Use the loan only for read-only operations inside this callback
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0201

Error [E0402]: This call can fail and nothing checks it
  --> expiring_secret_loan_rejects_move_variadic_and_drop_paths.jet:12:9
    |
 12 |         consume(^borrowed)
    |         ^^^^^^^
 Why: A fallible result can't be ignored — handle it or say failure is impossible
 Fix: Use `?`, `??`, `panic ...`, or `.drop("reason")` to intentionally discard
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0402

Error [E0113]: This value is Int (a whole number), but `run` returns Err!
  --> expiring_secret_loan_rejects_move_variadic_and_drop_paths.jet:13:16
    |
 13 |         return 0
    |                ^
 Why: `run` declares Err! as its result, so the value it hands back must be Err!
 Fix: Hand back a Err! value: convert this value to Err!, or return the value you meant
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0113

Error [E2402]: This implicit fallible call can't convert `Expired` into `Err` — no declared conversion exists
  --> expiring_secret_loan_rejects_move_variadic_and_drop_paths.jet:11:17
    |
 11 |     _ := secret.with((borrowed) -> {
    |                 ^^^^
 Why: Ordinary fallible calls propagate automatically; `Expired` can reach `Err` only through `impl Expired -> Err`
 Fix: Handle this call locally with `??`, add `impl Expired -> Err { … }`, or change the return type
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2402
